                <pb facs="0194" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/14.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Beaupré to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The
                            Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-04-11"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 11, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Beaupré asks if permission has been obtained from Belgium for the transit of
                    Nicholas Knepper in accordance with article 4 of the Belgian law of 1874.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
